han one nucleus.\")\n5969:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Multinucleate\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000228 \"multinucleated cells\")\n5970:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Multinucleate\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000228 \"polynuclear cells\")\n5976:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000229 \"OBSOLETE (was not defined before being made obsolete).\")\n5977:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000229 \"Refers to an activated mature lymphocyte phenotype rather than a distinct cell type; consider using 'lymphocyte ; CL:0000542' or one of its children instead.\")\n5983:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000230 \"OBSOLETE (was not defined before being made obsolete).\")\n5984:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000230 \"Refers to an activated mature T lymphocyte phenotype rather than a distinct cell type; consider using 'T cell ; CL:0000084' or one of its children instead.\")\n5990:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000231 \"OBSOLETE (was not defined before being made obsolete).\")\n5991:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000231 \"Refers to an activated mature B lymphocyte phenotype rather than a distinct cell type; consider using 'B cell ; CL:0000236' or one of its children instead.\")\n5997:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D004912\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000232 \"A red blood cell. In mammals, mature erythrocytes are biconcave disks containing hemoglobin whose function is to transport oxygen.\")\n5998:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000232 \"BTO:0000424\")\n5999:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000232 \"CALOHA:TS-0290\")\n6000:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000232 \"FMA:81100\")\n6001:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000232 \"RBC\")\n6002:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000232 \"red blood cell\")\n6010: