cell that is part of some outer medullary collecting duct. It is known in some mammalian species that this cell may contribute in the maintenance of acid/base homeostasis.\")\n27950:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000717 \"KUPO:0001133\")\n27959:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000718 \"KUPO:0001134\")\n27968:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000719 \"KUPO:0001135\")\n27977:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000720 \"KUPO:0001136\")\n27986:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000721 \"KUPO:0001137\")\n27995:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1152/physrev.1998.78.3.723>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intraglomerular_mesangial_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000742 \"A mesangial cell located among the glomerular capillaries in a renal corpuscle.\")\n27996:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000742 \"KUPO:0001032\")\n27997:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:cjm\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_1000742 \"intraglomerular mesangial cell\")\n27998:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9127003\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1152/physrev.1998.78.3.723\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_1000742 \"Like smooth muscle, a glomerular mesangial cell is contractile and possesses the filaments actin and myosin. The contractile mechanism is also similar to that of smooth muscle, with Ca2+/calmodulin-activated myosin light-chain kinase instigating myosin-actin cross-bridge cycling. Mesangial cell phagocytosis of apoptotic neutrophils involves a novel CD36-independent, alpha(v)beta3/TSP-mediated mechanism that is uncoupled from chemokine secretion, emphasizing the injury-limiting potential of mesangial cell phagocytosis of apoptotic cells.\")\n28008:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000746 \"KUPO:0001036\")\n28014:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000768 \"KUPO:0001058\")\n28023:AnnotationA